    "section_number": "5.2.2",
    "section_heading": "Re-Admission",
    "parent_section_heading": "STUDENT LIFE",
    "content": "1. Unless students are away on an approved leave of absence when they resume, they should apply for re-admission and pay a non-refundable application processing fee.\n2. Leave of absence is allowed for a maximum of one academic year (i.e., three semesters).\n3. Students who are re-admitted will be treated as new students and the Dean or designee will evaluate their transcripts based on current curriculum and admission requirements.",
